From: Paresh Dudhat <129591319+dudhatparesh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:21:27 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(desktop): work claims, who is working on an issue
 (terminalx#441)

A desktop publishes the sessions it has linked to tracker issues, per
device, and the Issues list reads the claims its reader may see.

- PUT /v1/desktop/work-claims/devices/:deviceId replaces the device's set
  in one transaction, serialized per device with an advisory lock: a
  session left out is withdrawn, `since` survives a refresh of the same
  issue, and the caller's expired rows go. Strict bodies: an unknown key
  anywhere (a prompt, a transcript) fails with work_claims_invalid_request.
- DELETE of the same path withdraws the device (sign-out).
- GET /v1/desktop/work-claims?provider=&scope= lists the caller's own
  claims with device and session, and a teammate's only through a shared
  non-personal organization with work status on that connected the
  claim's repository (an accessible selected repository, or an `all`
  installation of its owner), with no device or session. Membership is
  read in the query on every request.
- GET|POST /v1/desktop/orgs/:orgId/work-status is the organization
  switch; the service checks membership (404) and owner/admin (403), and a
  personal organization has none (400).
- Capability account.work-claims.v1 on every desktop session body.

Migration 0095 adds issue_work_claims and
organization_work_status_settings. Contract: apps/api/docs/work-claims.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
