+# Work claims v1 (terminalx#441)
+
+The server half of "show who is working on an issue across machines and
+teammates in the Issues list". A _work claim_ says: this person has a session
+on this device (or in a cloud workspace) linked to this tracker issue, in this
+state, last active at this time. The desktop publishes the full set of its
+claims per device; the Issues list on any desktop reads the claims visible to
+its reader for the issues it shows.
+
+## What leaves the machine (and nothing else)
+
+The issue reference (provider, id, identifier, scope), the person (from the
+token, never from the body), a device id and label, a session id, the session
+title, the branch name, a coarse state, the project's normalised remote, two
+booleans (`cloud`, `shareWithTeam`) and idle seconds. Never prompts, transcript
+content, file paths, diffs or code. Every body is parsed strictly: an unknown
+key at the top level, in a claim or in its issue fails the whole request with
+400, so a field added by mistake on the desktop fails loudly instead of being
+stored. Request bodies under `/v1/desktop/work-claims/*` carry the
+`requestBodyLoggingPolicy: redacted` marker, like the pairing routes.
+
+## Capability
+
+`POST /v1/desktop/auth/capabilities` and every desktop session body built by
+`buildDesktopSessionBody` report `flags["account.work-claims.v1"] = true`.
+Mobile capability bodies never carry it (the routes take desktop tokens only).
+A desktop that does not see the flag never calls the routes below and shows
+"shared work status unavailable".
+
+## Keys
+
+- `scope`: where the issue lives, from the issue URL, lower case.
+    - GitHub: `github.com/<owner>/<repo>` (from
+      `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<n>`).
+    - Linear: `linear.app/<workspace url key>` (from
+      `https://linear.app/<workspace>/issue/ENG-42/...`).
+- `issue.identifier`: `#441` on GitHub; `ENG-42` (upper case) on Linear.
+  Readers match on (provider, scope, identifier).
+- `repository`: the normalised remote of the project the session runs in,
+  lower case, no scheme, no user info, no `.git`: `github.com/acme/widgets`.
+  Null when the project has no remote. Used only to decide whether teammates
+  may see the claim; never returned.
+
+## Routes
+
+All under `/v1/desktop`, behind `desktopAuth` (a desktop access token;
+otherwise 401 `{ "error": "unauthorized" }`), JSON, and every answer, errors
+included, carries `Cache-Control: no-store`. Errors are `{ "error": "<code>" }`
+(`desktopError`). An unexpected failure answers 500
+`work_claims_internal_error` and logs only the error, never the request.
+
+### `PUT /work-claims/devices/:deviceId`
+
+Replaces the caller's claim set for this device. `deviceId` matches
+`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,64}$` (the desktop sends its pairing host id, 16
+characters). The body is at most 256 KiB (a larger one answers 400
+`work_claims_invalid_request` before it is read).
+
+```json
+{
+    "deviceLabel": "Studio Mac",
+    "claims": [
+        {
+            "sessionId": "8c1e…",
+            "scope": "github.com/acme/widgets",
+            "repository": "github.com/acme/widgets",
+            "issue": {
+                "provider": "github",
+                "id": "441",
+                "identifier": "#441"
+            },
+            "title": "#441 Show who is working on an issue",
+            "branch": "raccoon/441-show-who-is-working",
+            "state": "working",
+            "cloud": false,
+            "shareWithTeam": true,
+            "idleSeconds": 42
+        }
+    ]
+}
+```
+
+Validation (400 `work_claims_invalid_request` on any failure, including bad
+JSON, a bad `deviceId` and an unknown key anywhere):
+
+- The body has exactly `deviceLabel` and `claims`; `claims` is an array of 0
+  to 100 claims with unique `sessionId`s. An empty array withdraws every claim
+  of the device.
+- `deviceLabel`: string, trimmed, 1–80 characters (code points), no control
+  characters (`\p{Cc}`).
+- Each claim has exactly the keys above. `repository` and `branch` may be
+  `null` or left out (read as `null`); every other key is required.
+- `sessionId`: 1–160 characters of `[A-Za-z0-9_.:/-]`.
+- `scope`, lower-cased first: `^github\.com/[a-z0-9-]{1,39}/[a-z0-9._-]{1,100}$`
+  when the issue provider is github, `^linear\.app/[a-z0-9-]{1,64}$` when it
+  is linear. A scope of the other provider's kind is refused.
+- `repository`: null, or lower-cased
+  `^[a-z0-9.-]{1,253}(:[0-9]{1,5})?(/[a-z0-9._~-]{1,100}){1,8}$`, at most 300
+  characters.
+- `issue` has exactly `provider` (`github` | `linear`), `id` (1–128 characters
+  of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`) and `identifier`: `^#[0-9]{1,10}$` on GitHub,
+  `^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{0,9}-[0-9]{1,10}$` on Linear (upper-cased first).
+- `title`: string, trimmed, 1–200 characters (code points), no control
+  characters.
+- `branch`: null, or 1–255 characters with no whitespace (`\s`) and no control
+  characters.
+- `state`: `working` (an agent turn runs) | `waiting` (an agent waits on the
+  person) | `idle` | `pull_request` (idle, with an open pull request).
+- `cloud`, `shareWithTeam`: booleans. `idleSeconds`: integer 0–2592000.
+
+Semantics, in one transaction, serialized per (user, device) with a
+transaction advisory lock so two concurrent publishes from one device can never
+leave the union of both:
+
+- Rows of this (user, device) whose `sessionId` is not in the body are deleted
+  (withdrawal: archive, delete, unlink, private session, closed issue, merged
+  pull request all arrive as "not in the set").
+- Each claim is upserted on (user, device, sessionId), with the label of the
+  body: `last_active_at = now - idleSeconds`, `refreshed_at = now`,
+  `expires_at = now + 24 h`. `since` is kept from the existing row when its
+  (provider, scope, identifier) is the same, else `now`.
+- The caller's expired rows (any device) are deleted.
+
+After the commit, every expired row (anyone's) is deleted too, best effort;
+expired rows are never returned, so this only keeps the table small.
+
+Response 200:
+
+```json
+{ "claims": 1, "refreshAfterSeconds": 120, "liveForSeconds": 300 }
+```
+
+`claims` is the number stored for this device.
+
+### `DELETE /work-claims/devices/:deviceId`
+
+Withdraws every claim of this (user, device), under the same per-device lock.
+Sent on sign-out. Response 200 `{ "claims": 0 }`. A bad `deviceId` answers 400
+`work_claims_invalid_request`.
+
+### `GET /work-claims?provider=github&scope=github.com/acme/widgets[&scope=…]`
+
+`provider` is required exactly once; 1–10 `scope` values, each lower-cased
+and validated against the provider as above (duplicates after lower-casing
+are read once). Any other query parameter is ignored. A failure answers 400
+`work_claims_invalid_request`. Returns the claims visible to the caller,
+newest activity first (`last_active_at` descending), at most 500:
+
+```json
+{
+    "now": 1793232000000,
+    "liveForSeconds": 300,
+    "claims": [
+        {
+            "scope": "github.com/acme/widgets",
+            "issue": {
+                "provider": "github",
+                "id": "441",
+                "identifier": "#441"
+            },
+            "person": { "name": "Alice Example", "you": false },
+            "device": null,
+            "sessionId": null,
+            "title": "#441 Show who is working on an issue",
+            "branch": "alice/441-work-status",
+            "state": "working",
+            "cloud": false,
+            "live": true,
+            "since": 1793230000000,
+            "lastActiveAt": 1793231900000,
+            "refreshedAt": 1793231990000
+        }
+    ]
+}
+```
+
+- All times are epoch milliseconds on the server's clock; `now` lets the
+  reader compute ages without trusting its own clock.
+  `live` = `refreshed_at > now - 300 s`.
+- Only rows with `expires_at > now` and `last_active_at > now - 24 h`.
+- `person.name`: `users.name` (trimmed), else the part of the email before
+  `@`. Never the email itself, never the user id.
+- `device` (`{ "id", "label" }`) and `sessionId` are filled only on the
+  caller's own claims (`you: true`). Machine names are shown only to their
+  owner. `repository` and `shareWithTeam` are never returned.
+
+Visibility:
+
+1. The caller's own claims, from every device: always.
+2. Another person's claim, only when **all** hold:
+    - the claim has `share_with_team = true` and a non-null `repository`;
+    - there is an organization O with `is_personal = false` of which both the
+      caller and the claim's owner are members (read in the same query on
+      every request, never cached);
+    - O's work status sharing is on
+      (`organization_work_status_settings.share_work_status`, true when no
+      row);
+    - the claim's repository belongs to O:
+      `repository = 'github.com/' || lower(full_name)` of an
+      `organization_github_repositories` row of O in state `accessible`, or
+      its host (first segment) is `github.com` and its
+      owner (second segment) equals `lower(account_login)` of a `connected`
+      `organization_github_installations` row of O with
+      `repository_selection = 'all'`.
+
+Someone outside every such organization sees nothing; a personal project (a
+repository no shared organization connected) is never shown to anyone else.
+
+### `GET /orgs/:orgId/work-status` and `POST /orgs/:orgId/work-status`
+
+The organization switch for admins. `desktopAuth`; not a `member`-middleware
+route: the service reads the caller's membership itself on every request,
+like `orgMembers.ts`. A non-member (or an unknown organization) answers 404
+`not_found`.
+
+- GET → `{ "shareWorkStatus": true, "canManage": true, "personal": false }`.
+  `canManage` is true for an owner or admin of a non-personal organization. A
+  personal organization never shares, so it answers
+  `{ "shareWorkStatus": false, "canManage": false, "personal": true }`.
+- POST `{ "shareWorkStatus": false }` (exactly that key, a boolean; body at
+  most 1 KiB). Checked in this order: non-member 404 `not_found`; not owner or
+  admin 403 `forbidden`; personal organization 400
+  `work_status_personal_organization`; a bad body (or one over 1 KiB) 400
+  `work_claims_invalid_request`. Stores the switch with `updated_by` and
+  `updated_at`, and answers like GET.
+
+## Storage
+
+Migration `0095_issue_work_claims.sql` is additive: two new tables, nothing
+existing is rewritten or backfilled.
+
+- `issue_work_claims`: `id`, `user_id` (FK users, cascade), `device_id`,
+  `device_label`, `session_id`, `scope`, `repository`, `issue_provider`,
+  `issue_id`, `issue_identifier`, `title`, `branch`, `state`, `cloud`,
+  `share_with_team`, `since`, `last_active_at`, `refreshed_at`, `expires_at`,
+  `created_at`, `updated_at`. Unique (user_id, device_id, session_id); indexes
+  on (scope, issue_provider), (user_id) and (expires_at); CHECK constraints on
+  `state` and `issue_provider`.
+- `organization_work_status_settings`: `organization_id` (PK, FK
+  organizations, cascade), `share_work_status` (default true), `updated_by`
+  (FK users, set null), `updated_at`.
+
+Deleting a user deletes their claims; deleting an organization deletes its
+switch. Rollback: deploy the prior server first (the tables may stay); to drop
+the schema afterwards, drop `issue_work_claims` and
+`organization_work_status_settings`. Both hold only ephemeral status, so
+nothing of value is lost.
+
+The windows are named constants in `src/lib/constants/workClaims.ts`:
+retention 24 h (`retentionSeconds`), live window 300 s (`liveForSeconds`),
+refresh 120 s (`refreshAfterSeconds`).
+
+## Desktop behaviour (for reference; implemented in the terminalx repo)
+
+- Publishes on session create, link change, status transitions, debounced
+  (~3 s), plus a heartbeat every 120 s; withdraws by publishing without the
+  claim; `DELETE` on sign-out.
+- A claim is "working now" only while `live` and its state is
+  working/waiting, or it was active in the last 30 minutes; otherwise "was
+  working on this, <age> ago"; hidden after 24 h without activity.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `src/services/workClaims/validation.test.ts`: every validation rule above,
+  unknown keys (`prompt`, `transcript`, …) at the top level, per claim and in
+  the issue, scope/provider mismatch, identifier formats, limits, the list
+  query and the switch body.
+- `src/controllers/desktop/workClaims.test.ts`: the routes through the real
+  desktop router with the service and the token resolver mocked: shapes,
+  normalised input reaching the service, `Cache-Control: no-store` on success
+  and error, 401 without a desktop session, the 256 KiB limit, error codes.
+- `src/routes/desktop.test.ts`: the work status routes are dispatched to their
+  own controller and are not membership-marked.
+- `src/controllers/desktop/buildDesktopSession.test.ts`: the capability flag
+  on every desktop body and never on mobile.
+- `src/services/workClaims/workClaims.integration.test.ts` (isolated Postgres,
+  `WORK_CLAIMS_TEST_DATABASE_URL`): own claims across devices with device and
+  session; a teammate through a selected accessible repository and through an
+  `all` installation, with no device or session; a suspended installation, a
+  `missing` repository row and unconnected repositories hidden; an outsider
+  sees nothing; a personal organization never shares; `shareWithTeam: false`
+  and a null repository kept to the owner; the switch off hides and on shows
+  again; a removed member stops seeing at once; replace withdraws missing
+  sessions; `since` kept on refresh and reset when the issue changes;
+  `live` false from 300 s; expiry at 24 h after refresh or of activity;
+  expired rows pruned; DELETE; concurrent publishes from one device; the
+  500-row cap; the switch's 404/403/400 answers and its personal case.
+- `src/db/migrationJournal.test.ts`: the journal entry is applied after 0094.
