From 1615d7c4fc9f86548cbe0af001fbd1cfee25f013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paresh Dudhat <129591319+dudhatparesh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:18:08 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(desktop): work claims follow the issue's
 organization, with limits (terminalx#441)

Review of 6c86414.

- Visibility follows where the issue lives. GitHub: the claim's scope (the
  issue's repository) must be connected to the shared organization, so work
  in a personal fork on an organization issue shows and an organization
  repository is no longer a way to show an unrelated issue. Linear: the
  scope's workspace must be one the organization's admins declared, and the
  claim's repository must be connected, so a personal project never shows.
- organization_work_status_settings.linear_workspaces (text[], default {});
  GET /orgs/:orgId/work-status answers linearWorkspaces, and POST takes
  shareWorkStatus and/or linearWorkspaces (at most 10, lower-cased,
  deduplicated), keeping what is not sent.
- Device ids are bounded: a non-empty PUT for a new device while 10 others
  have live claims answers 409 work_claims_device_limit, under a per-person
  lock taken only by a joining device. PUT is limited to one per device
  every 2 s (429 work_claims_rate_limited with Retry-After), on the
  rate_limits lanes the Host binding heartbeat uses. A read returns at most
  50 claims per person.
- Every claim carries an opaque key, sha256(user id + session id), equal for
  one person's cloud session published from two Macs.
- The replace transaction no longer deletes other devices' expired rows; the
  prune after the commit does.

Migration 0095 is edited in place (not merged anywhere).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
