+Limits, checked after validation:
+
+- **Rate**: one PUT per (person, device) every 2 seconds. A sooner one answers
+  429 `work_claims_rate_limited` with `Retry-After: <whole seconds>` (1 or 2)
+  and changes nothing. It uses the `rate_limits` lanes of the Host binding
+  heartbeat (`checkAccountPairingRateLimit`, subject hashed, operation
+  `work-claims-publish`). DELETE is not limited.
+- **Devices**: a non-empty PUT for a device with no unexpired claim, while the
+  person has unexpired claims on 10 other device ids, answers 409
+  `work_claims_device_limit` and changes nothing. An empty PUT
+  (`"claims": []`) is never refused by this limit; for a new device it stores
+  nothing. A device that already has unexpired claims may always refresh
+  them. The check runs under a per-person lock taken after the device's,
+  only by a joining device, so devices joining at once cannot pass it
+  together.
+
 Semantics, in one transaction, serialized per (user, device) with a
 transaction advisory lock so two concurrent publishes from one device can never
 leave the union of both:
 
 - Rows of this (user, device) whose `sessionId` is not in the body are deleted
   (withdrawal: archive, delete, unlink, private session, closed issue, merged
-  pull request all arrive as "not in the set").
+  pull request all arrive as "not in the set"), expired or not.
